templates
T:call-context-manager-capture = Context Manager: Capture the reasoning and conclusions from this discussion. What connections were drawn? What hypotheses were formed or rejected? What decisions were made about what to investigate next? Preserve the logic chain. If any leads or open questions were identified but not yet pursued, mark them with [LEAD]. Aim for about # tokens.
T:call-context-manager-cm-recall = Context Manager: [CM] Recall memory L#-#.
T:call-context-manager-cm-the = Context Manager: [CM] The conversation resumes.
T:call-context-manager-please = Context Manager: Please consolidate these # L# summaries (# synthesis) into a single cohesive memory. Aim for about # tokens. Write as you would to yourself — this is your autobiography, capturing the arc of what happened. IMPORTANT: Preserve any items marked with [LEAD] — these are unresolved questions that must survive consolidation until explicitly resolved or dropped.
T:call-context-manager-system = Context Manager: System: You will soon form a new memory, get ready. The messages that follow are the slice of recent experience you are about to compress. After them, write the memory in your own voice.
T:call-context-manager-you = Context Manager: You have just reviewed the L# memories above, in chronological order. They cover the stretch of experience you are about to consolidate into a single L# memory. Write a memory that preserves the through-line: what happened, what was decided, what remains open, what concrete details future you will want to reach for. Speak in the first person. Target ~# tokens. Output only the memory body — no preamble, no meta-commentary about summarizing.
T:call-empty = 
  
  ---
  
  
T:call-user-launch-of = user: Launch of spawn 'knowledge-#', as resolved at its subagent--spawn call:
  - Lineage: spawned by stream "fixture" as a separate agent with its own system prompt and task; it inherits none of the caller's context; depth # of #.
  - Model: claude-opus-#-#, the same as the caller's.
  - Provider: anthropic, on the same connection as the caller's.
  - System prompt: supplied by the caller for this spawn.
  - Strategy: a fresh knowledge instance (the caller's: autobiographical).
  - Head window: #,# tokens (the caller's isn't reported).
  - Recent window: #,# tokens (the caller's: #,# tokens).
  - Message cap: #,# tokens, the same as the caller's.
  - Compression model: claude-opus-#-# (the caller's isn't reported).
  - Context budget: not set by this launch, so the framework's default for a new stream applies, stated when the stream starts (the caller's: #,# tokens).
  - Stream budget: #,# tokens (the caller's: #,# tokens).
  - Output limit: #,# tokens, the same as the caller's.
  - Prose routing: locus, inherited from the caller: plain text is published to the channel the framework infers for each turn, if there is one.
  - Tool rules: no restriction, the same as the caller.
  At the start of this stream:
  - Inherited: nothing; a spawn starts from its task.
  - Context budget: #,# tokens (the caller's at the call: #,# tokens).
  - Agent settings not carried from the calling stream, so the framework's defaults apply: clock rows off (the calling stream's: every # minutes). The rest match: extended thinking, provider parameters, prompt caching, prompt-cache TTL, prefill user message, same-round think-text policy, refusal handling, tool-result guard, tool-wrapper prose guard and auto-continue.
  - Tools: # available to this stream: time--now, subagent--spawn, subagent--fork, subagent--hud, subagent--concurrency, subagent--peek, subagent--list, subagent--stop, subagent--message, subagent--adopt, subagent--resume, subagent--return, toolsets--open, toolsets--act, toolsets--look, toolsets--close, mcpl--fixture--result, channel_list, channel_open, channel_decline, channel_close, channel_publish, think, journal, skip_reply and drafts.
